body:
This is an issue with the implementation of `DirAccess::is_equivalent` on windows. Since I'm not on windows I can't look into this.

If any of you has a setup to build Godot, feel free to try this very hypothetical patch: 

```patch
diff --git a/drivers/windows/dir_access_windows.cpp b/drivers/windows/dir_access_windows.cpp
index 73df578cf8..eefac55e6f 100644
--- a/drivers/windows/dir_access_windows.cpp
+++ b/drivers/windows/dir_access_windows.cpp
@@ -416,7 +416,6 @@ bool DirAccessWindows::is_equivalent(const String &p_path_a, const String &p_pat
 		return DirAccess::is_equivalent(p_path_a, p_path_b);
 	}
 	::GetFileInformationByHandleEx(h1, (FILE_INFO_BY_HANDLE_CLASS)0x12 /*FileIdInfo*/, &st1, sizeof(st1));
-	::CloseHandle(h1);

 	String f2 = fix_path(p_path_b);
 	GD_FILE_ID_INFO st2;
@@ -425,9 +424,13 @@ bool DirAccessWindows::is_equivalent(const String &p_path_a, const String &p_pat
 		return DirAccess::is_equivalent(p_path_a, p_path_b);
 	}
 	::GetFileInformationByHandleEx(h2, (FILE_INFO_BY_HANDLE_CLASS)0x12 /*FileIdInfo*/, &st2, sizeof(st2));
+
+	bool res = (st1.VolumeSerialNumber == st2.VolumeSerialNumber) && (st1.FileId.LowPart == st2.FileId.LowPart) && (st1.FileId.HighPart == st2.FileId.HighPart);
+
+	::CloseHandle(h1);
 	::CloseHandle(h2);

-	return (st1.VolumeSerialNumber == st2.VolumeSerialNumber) && (st1.FileId.LowPart == st2.FileId.LowPart) && (st1.FileId.HighPart == st2.FileId.HighPart);
+	return res;
 }

 bool DirAccessWindows::is_link(String p_file) {

```

If that does not help I'd recommend opening a new issue which leaves the language server aside and provides a simple MRP for the malfunctioning method. Maybe this I'll get better attention from some folks who actually work on windows.

